usage: evolution [-h]
                 {init,cycle,experiment,governance,final,full-self-evolution,meta,verify-ledger,preview,registry,capability-audit,freeze-protocol,develop,promote,smoke,capability-smoke,archive,sandbox-check,metamorphic-gate} ...

Intervention-based self-evolution framework for detector.

positional arguments:
  {init,cycle,experiment,governance,final,full-self-evolution,meta,verify-ledger,preview,registry,capability-audit,freeze-protocol,develop,promote,smoke,capability-smoke,archive,sandbox-check,metamorphic-gate}
    cycle               run one evolution cycle
    experiment          run multiple evolution cycles
    governance          post-cycle attribution, retirement and rollback
                        accounting
    final               evaluate an explicitly configured independent sealed
                        holdout
    full-self-evolution
                        run evolution and evaluate the disjoint sealed holdout
    meta                meta-evaluation of the evolution mechanism
    verify-ledger       verify append-only ledger hash chain
    preview             patrol and draft proposals without spending gate
                        budget
    registry            show active registry
    capability-audit    report the executable evolution surface and its hard
                        limits
    freeze-protocol     freeze a candidate-unused promotion batch before any
                        model call
    develop             develop a candidate for one mechanism: draft, L0,
                        targeted L1 replay, revise, freeze
    promote             carry a frozen candidate through the deployment gates
    smoke               offline one-cycle gate validation
    capability-smoke    offline self-evolution gain validation with a new
                        typed-DSL predicate
    archive             show the candidate archive and component store
                        (--ingest archives one development run)
    sandbox-check       report the Level B sandbox limits and escape-route
                        refusals (--probe makes a real child violate each
                        limit)
    metamorphic-gate    run the six §15.2 metamorphic relations against the
                        registered runners and report each admission verdict

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
